MID_SE_Gat_Dan_C: <EDH>
MID_SE_Gat_Dan_C_001: Hrm. Hrrrmmm.
MID_SE_Gat_Dan_C_002: Don't stare like that, Dante. It's uncouth.
MID_SE_Gat_Dan_C_003: But your poise and elegance demand my attention.
MID_SE_Gat_Dan_C_004: You keep your back straight and a regular stride.\nYou're like no gladiator I know.
MID_SE_Gat_Dan_C_005: You are, what's the word...venerable! You are much\nlike a bronze statue coated in verdigris.
MID_SE_Gat_Dan_C_006: What truly lies beneath that rusted form? Are there\nbold colors emblazoned where none can see?
MID_SE_Gat_Dan_C_007: You have a keener eye than I credited you with.\nYour powers of observation rival Bertrand's.
MID_SE_Gat_Dan_C_008: Ohoho! Is it any wonder? There's no judge of\ncharacter quite like me, the master auteur!
MID_SE_Gat_Dan_C_009: Answer me this, if you will. From what clarion spring\ndoes your elegance spout?
MID_SE_Gat_Dan_C_010: Are you noble by nature? Or did you adopt a noble\nbearing through diligent work?
MID_SE_Gat_Dan_C_011: Hmm. If I had to chalk it up to one thing, I think it\nwould be my days as a knight errant.
MID_SE_Gat_Dan_C_012: As a younger man, I spent about three years in the\nland of Sai, where they beat the insolence out of me.
MID_SE_Gat_Dan_C_013: I've heard tell of the place. A fabulous land far\nto the east!
MID_SE_Gat_Dan_C_014: A renowned warrior there looked after me. I stayed\nas his guest and spent my days training.
MID_SE_Gat_Dan_C_015: It was a land of strict decorum. I had no merit apart\nfrom skill at combat, so I was regularly disciplined.
MID_SE_Gat_Dan_C_016: They have their own advanced etiquette there. The\nmanners I learned in Dagda were no use at all.
MID_SE_Gat_Dan_C_017: Fascinating! There's no substitute for experience\nwhen it comes to absorbing another culture.
MID_SE_Gat_Dan_C_018: I must know more about Sai. What do they eat? How\ndo they dress? Whom do they worship?
MID_SE_Gat_Dan_C_019: Easy there. One question at a time, or we'll be here\nuntil tomorrow.
MID_SE_Gat_Dan_C_020: But there's so much I'm burning to know! Before,\nyou mentioned "the manners I learned in Dagda."
MID_SE_Gat_Dan_C_021: But there are so many cultures here that you could\nmean anything! I deal in specificities, good sir!
MID_SE_Gat_Dan_C_022: If I don't know where you hail from originally, how\ncan I compare it to where you've sojourned?!
MID_SE_Gat_Dan_C_023: Heh. Oh dear. I may be in over my head.
